# Names only; copy to .dev.vars (git-ignored, as are .dev.vars.* and .env*) and fill in values. Never commit values.
# Never put a production value here: the top-level and staging configs name the production SUPABASE_URL. Use local or test values only.
# BD-FIX-SEC-02: every deny-listed name of tools/ci/secret-env.ts in this file (all the secrets below) reaches no Worker by default:
# `pnpm dev` and `pnpm dev:edge` pass it on empty, `pnpm check:workers` binds it empty, and the e2e web server and check:pipeline read no
# env file at all. Only `DV_ALLOW_LIVE_SECRETS=1 pnpm dev:edge` (or `pnpm dev`) passes these values to the local Worker, with a warning.
# PLAY_TOKEN_HMAC = "<kid>:<base64url of 32 random bytes>", e.g. "k1:" + `openssl rand -base64 32 | tr '+/' '-_' | tr -d '='`
PLAY_TOKEN_HMAC=
# PLAY_TOKEN_HMAC_PREV=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
OPS_TOKEN=
FAL_KEY=
# M06a1: salts the daily network hash of the per-net caps (any random string; absent: the UTC day alone, which still works locally)
QUOTA_NET_SALT_SECRET=
# M06a3: `pnpm dev` already runs the Worker on recorded streams (--var ANTHROPIC_MODE:fixture). For `pnpm dev:edge`, or to call the real model, set these
# (.dev.vars overrides the wrangler vars). Live mode needs the key of the Anthropic workspace npc-runtime; AIG_BASE is the gateway gw-dialogue, unset = direct API.
# The key reaches the Worker only with DV_ALLOW_LIVE_SECRETS=1 (see the top of this file).
# ANTHROPIC_MODE=fixture
# FLAGS_JSON={"npc.dialogue":true}
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# AIG_BASE=
